=== P3 Shared surface 0004 AIAlertTuningSuggestions (Android) ===
Web source : web/src/components/ai/AIAlertTuningSuggestions.tsx
Native out : apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/AIAlertTuningSuggestions.kt
Package    : com.teslasync.sharedsurfaces

Implementation: native Jetpack Compose / Material 3 surface authored at parity with the web
source. Reproduced behaviour, branch-for-branch with the web component:
  * withAiFeature off-mode gate -> surface is ABSENT (renders nothing) when aiFeatureEnabled is
    false (ADR-015 §I5). Root carries testTag "ai-feature-alert-tuning-suggestions-root".
  * AIFeatureCard scaffold (header + Helix badge + descriptive subtitle + below-placed action +
    output region + typed-proposal children slot) reproduced with Material 3 primitives — the web
    AIFeatureCard/AiOutputPanel/withAiFeature trio has no dedicated Android component prompt, so
    the scaffold is composed inline from platform primitives per the Android-HIG instruction
    ("native primitives, not web Tailwind").
  * Computed disabled (web Rule W1-A): computeCanStart(ruleId, phase) + AiFeatureStream.isBusy
    gate both buttons — never a literal disabled flag.
  * tool_result capture: extractAlertRulePatch() folds the draft_alert_rule_patch frame into the
    typed AlertRuleDraftPatch field-for-field (numbers only when numeric, strings only when
    non-blank), mirroring the web handleEvent capture exactly. Pure + public so the prompt's
    adapter unit test can target it without composing the view.
  * No direct I/O from the view: the SSE start / cancel-on-ruleId-change / proposal-reset
    lifecycle lives in the injected P1/S8 holder; the view consumes a folded AiFeatureStream +
    captured proposal and calls onSuggest / onApplyDraft (the AlertStudio editor merge). The panel
    NEVER persists — the canonical AlertStudio Save button remains the sole write path
    (ADR-015 §I3 + §I8).
  * States reproduced (the branches the web source actually renders): gated-off (absent), idle,
    streaming (spinner + "Helix is thinking…"), error (polite failure text; the Suggest button is
    the retry affordance), done-with-proposal (review list + Apply to form), done-without-proposal
    (no preview). The generic prompt-checklist "stale"/"offline" states do NOT apply: an AI stream
    is not a cache-then-network Resource feed, and the web source has no stale/offline branch.
  * i18n: every visible string resolves through the P1/S10 facade (stringRes -> translation_*
    catalog). All keys already present in res/values/strings.xml:
      translation_notifications_alertStudio_aiTuning_{title,description,suggestButton,applyButton,previewLabel,badge}
      translation_chatbot_thinking, translation_queryError_title
    The proposed-patch field identifiers (value_num, cooldown_min, …) are rendered verbatim as
    technical keys, matching the web source which does not translate them.
  * Accessibility: action buttons carry stateDescription + testTag; 48dp Material touch targets;
    theme-token colours (no hardcoded web hex) so dark/light + font-scale follow the A1 theme.
  * view.opened diagnostics event emitted via TrackSurfaceView(slug="AIAlertTuningSuggestions")
    (P1/S11). No TODO/stub/mock/placeholder/Lorem in shipped code.

