    from Google's Maven (dl.google.com / maven.google.com), which is DNS-blocked on this runner:
    "Could not resolve host: dl.google.com". Maven Central / Gradle Plugin Portal are reachable
    but do not host AGP/Compose/AndroidX. Per the operator directive, the predecessor-gate is
    explicitly bypassed for this sandbox: the Android toolchain cannot resolve here and the build
    is verified by other agents / the ADR-012 CI matrix on a runner with Google Maven access.
  * The P3 Android app scaffold + theme + DI predecessors (A0/A1/A3/A5/A6) are produced
    concurrently; this surface references their published APIs (com.teslasync.android.theme.*,
    com.teslasync.android.di.* via the shared TrackSurfaceView, com.teslasync.android.R) and the
    same-package shared scaffold (stringRes, TrackSurfaceView). It compiles once those land.
    Build/test verification is deferred to CI (tracked in
